# Root Environment Variables
# This file documents environment variables used across the monorepo

## Development
# Set NODE_ENV=development for local development
# Set NODE_ENV=production for production builds

## AWS Configuration
# AWS_REGION: AWS region for all services (default: us-east-1)
# AWS_ACCOUNT_ID: Your AWS account ID

## Workspace-Specific
# See individual workspace .env.example files:
# - apps/web/.env.example - Frontend environment variables
# - apps/functions/.env.example - Lambda environment variables
# - infra/.env.example - CDK deployment configuration

## Security Notes
# - Never commit .env or .env.local files
# - Only commit .env.example files with placeholder values
# - Use AWS Secrets Manager for sensitive production values
# - Cognito IDs are obtained after running `pnpm --filter infra deploy`
